urrent green run is not evidence that it stays green.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-agent/tests/xai.rs","range":{"start":89,"end":97}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/xai_api.rs","range":{"start":187,"end":198}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-workspace-advisory","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:51b849b76d9c99ba53bb8c44cb2e4b0ffac8a8ec82000222b58c9687fbf013de","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":92983,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-61","revision":"sha256:17509570806bbdc7395db3096bb30eeddb0313748438b7ca07065f8f6a280c86","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-51b849b76d9c99ba53bb8c44cb2e4b0ffac8a8ec82000222b58c9687fbf013de-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Remove environment mutation from the tests: make the credential source injectable at the adapter boundary (an `AuthDescriptor` variant or resolver closure the tests can supply directly), so `resolve_api_key`'s env path is exercised by one isolated test rather than by every adapter construction. If env mutation must stay, serialize those tests behind a shared mutex and give each a unique variable name.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"xai-runtime-not-shown-wired-into-any-dispatch-path","category":"unverifiable_claim","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"No change set evidence that a configured runtime = \"xai-api\" worker is actually dispatched to XaiAdapter at runtime","claim":"The contract document and `build_xai_adapter_from_config`'s doc comment both assert this is 'the link that makes a configured Grok worker reachable', but within the disclosed change set `build_xai_adapter_from_config` has no caller outside `#[cfg(test)]` code, and no file that selects or constructs an adapter for a worker's runtime id is modified — the only non-test, non-doc changes are two `mod`/`pub mod` declarations, a dev-dependency line, and `Cargo.lock`. I cannot confirm or refute the existence of a dispatch site because I am scoped to the disclosed package and must not inspect unrelated repository files, and the lint check was run with `-A dead-code`, so an unreachable constructor would not have been surfaced by verification either. As presented, the acceptance criterion that xAI is 'its own ProviderId with runtime xai-api' across routing and accounting paths is not demonstrated by anything in this change or its checks.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/xai_api.rs","range":{"start":92,"end":119}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"lint","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:b650a1002da5713fc2dce30ba93cfa354ac6a5045f8498beb69841f9485a0c80","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":1268,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-61","revision":"sha256:17509570806bbdc7395db3096bb30eeddb0313748438b7ca07065f8f6a280c86","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-b650a1002da5713fc2dce30ba93cfa354ac6a5045f8498beb69841f9485a0c80-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Either point to (or add) the production dispatch site that maps `runtime = \"xai-api\"` to `build_xai_adapter_from_config`, and cover it with a test that starts from a registry configuration and reaches a running `XaiAdapter` through the daemon's normal worker-construction path; or amend the contract document to state plainly that the constructor is not yet reachable from any runtime dispatch and name the PRD that will wire it.","status":"open","supersedes":null}]}
