{"review_id":"00001788308111360583-0004098830-000003-cycle-review-2","reviewed_manifest_hash":"sha256:97ad5dbe0908ac13e1ff5baa945da0e2fe3d7da6ea37497baaa2ace71733c151","findings":[{"finding_id":"xai-sse-utf8-chunk-boundary-corruption","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"high","blocking":false,"title":"SSE UTF-8 chunk-boundary corruption is fixed by byte-buffered line draining","claim":"The candidate replaces the lossy per-chunk `String::from_utf8_lossy` accumulation with a raw `Vec<u8>` buffer and `drain_complete_lines`, which decodes only fully assembled lines and leaves any trailing incomplete byte sequence in the buffer for the next transport chunk, returning `AdapterError::Ambiguous` on genuinely invalid UTF-8 rather than silently substituting U+FFFD. Two new unit tests (`drain_complete_lines_reassembles_multibyte_text_delta_split_across_chunks` and `..._tool_call_arguments_split_across_chunks`) split a 4-byte emoji mid-sequence and assert both the reassembled line and the decoded `content`/`arguments` payloads round-trip exactly. The defect described in the prior finding is no longer present.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/xai_api.rs","range":{"start":481,"end":501}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:e1c124d0d05c05980974a9208558ec74e42000bd82b7bbac672f675e30bc4125","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":34586,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-61","revision":"sha256:4e09f050613c1addb12549b3757f0d3ffb55009a00b5536f52ba4ae417f4963a","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-e1c124d0d05c05980974a9208558ec74e42000bd82b7bbac672f675e30bc4125-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"No further action; the byte-buffered line drain and its two split-codepoint regression tests close this finding.","status":"resolved","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"xai-send-timeout-classified-as-unbilled-transport","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"A request timeout awaiting response headers is classified as unbilled TransientTransport, not Ambiguous","claim":"`submit` maps every error from `.send()` to `AdapterError::Retryable(RetryableKind::TransientTransport)` with the comment asserting \"Nothing has been billed if the request never reached the provider\". That assertion does not hold for the timeout case: the client is built with `Client::builder().timeout(request_timeout_secs)`, a total request deadline that also elapses after the request body has been fully transmitted and xAI has begun generating (and billing) a response whose headers simply have not arrived yet. `reqwest` reports that case as an error from `.send()` with `is_timeout() == true`, indistinguishable here from a DNS/connect/TLS failure because the closure discards the error. The mid-stream path correctly distinguishes it (`error.is_timeout()` -> `Ambiguous`), so the two halves of the same adapter disagree. The result is an attempt whose completion state is genuinely unknown being recorded as a clean, nothing-billed retryable transport failure with zero/unknown usage, contradicting the acceptance criterion that a timeout with unknown completion records ambiguous usage.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/xai_api.rs","range":{"start":526,"end":537}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:e1c124d0d05c05980974a9208558ec74e42000bd82b7bbac672f675e30bc4125","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":34586,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-61","revision":"sha256:4e09f050613c1addb12549b3757f0d3ffb55009a00b5536f52ba4ae417f4963a","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-e1c124d0d05c05980974a9208558ec74e42000bd82b7bbac672f675e30bc4125-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Inspect the `reqwest::Error` in the `.send()` mapping instead of discarding it: map `error.is_connect()` / `error.is_request()` (pre-transmission failures) to `Retryable(TransientTransport)` as today, and map `error.is_timeout()` to `AdapterError::Ambiguous { reason: \"xAI request timed out before any response headers arrived; completion status unknown\" }` so the attempt records ambiguous usage. Add a wiremock test that delays the response past `request_timeout_secs` and asserts `Ambiguous`, and update the error table in `docs/contracts/xai-adapter.md`, which currently states the same incorrect \"nothing was billed\" claim for all pre-response transport failures.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"xai-per-attempt-telemetry-in-adapter-global-state","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"Provider-resolved model and vendor cost are adapter-global last-writer-wins state, so they can be stale or misattributed","claim":"`last_resolved_model` and `last_cost_usd_ticks` are `Mutex` fields on `XaiAdapter` itself, written during whatever `submit` happens to run last and read afterwards through `last_resolved_model()` / `last_cost_usd_ticks()`. Neither is keyed by `AttemptId`, and neither is cleared at the start of a `submit`. Sequentially: attempt 1 completes and stores `cost_in_usd_ticks = 8000` and `model = grok-4-0709`; attempt 2 fails or times out before its usage chunk arrives; a caller that reads `last_cost_usd_ticks()` after attempt 2 receives 8000 and attributes attempt 1's vendor cost and resolved identity to attempt 2. Concurrently, `InferenceAdapter` takes `&self`, so one adapter shared across two in-flight executions of the same worker interleaves writes and returns the other attempt's resolved identity or cost. `SubmitOutcome` already carries per-attempt `provider_request_id`, so the per-attempt channel exists; these two values are the only observations routed around it. No test covers a second submit after a failed one, nor concurrent submits, so the green suite does not exercise either path.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/xai_api.rs","range":{"start":129,"end":139}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/xai_api.rs","range":{"start":164,"end":185}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:e1c124d0d05c05980974a9208558ec74e42000bd82b7bbac672f675e30bc4125","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":34586,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-61","revision":"sha256:4e09f050613c1addb12549b3757f0d3ffb55009a00b5536f52ba4ae417f4963a","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-e1c124d0d05c05980974a9208558ec74e42000bd82b7bbac672f675e30bc4125-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Carry both values per attempt rather than per adapter: either key the maps on `AttemptId` (`Mutex<BTreeMap<AttemptId, ...>>`, written under the submitting attempt's id and read by id), or reset both to `None` at the top of each `submit` so a failed attempt cannot inherit the previous one's values. Preferably, return the resolved model and vendor cost ticks on `SubmitOutcome` alongside `provider_request_id`, which is the channel the loop already attributes per attempt. Add a regression test asserting that a submit that ends before any usage chunk reports `None` cost rather than the prior attempt's ticks.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"xai-unparseable-schema-silently-degrades-to-any-object","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"low","blocking":false,"title":"An unparseable tool or structured-output JSON schema is silently replaced with an unconstrained `{\"type\":\"object\"}`","claim":"`build_request_body` parses `structured_output.json_schema` with `serde_json::from_str(...).unwrap_or_else(|_| json!({\"type\": \"object\"}))`, and `wire_tool` does the same for `tool.json_schema`. When the schema string does not parse, the adapter sends a schema that constrains nothing and the failure is invisible: xAI accepts the request, the model returns arbitrary JSON or arbitrary tool arguments, and the loop reports a normal completion — for the structured-output path, a `StopReason::Completed { structured_output: true }` whose payload was never constrained by the requested schema. The in-file comment claims the opposite behavior for this branch (\"If this shape is wrong for a given deployment, xAI returns 400, which this adapter reports as `NonRetryable(InvalidRequest)` rather than silently degrading to unstructured text\"); that reasoning covers a rejected wire shape, not a schema the adapter itself discarded before sending. A caller-configured malformed schema is a configuration error an operator can fix, so it should surface as one.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/xai_api.rs","range":{"start":321,"end":336}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/xai_api.rs","range":{"start":299,"end":309}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:e1c124d0d05c05980974a9208558ec74e42000bd82b7bbac672f675e30bc4125","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":34586,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-61","revision":"sha256:4e09f050613c1addb12549b3757f0d3ffb55009a00b5536f52ba4ae417f4963a","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-e1c124d0d05c05980974a9208558ec74e42000bd82b7bbac672f675e30bc4125-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Make `build_request_body` fallible and return `AdapterError::NonRetryable(NonRetryableKind::InvalidRequest)` when either a tool's `json_schema` or `structured_output.json_schema` fails to parse, so the operator sees 